/-- **ℓ = 6.** For every `k ≥ 6`, every 2-colouring of `[1, F(k,6) + 10]` (here `natv q6F k = F(k,6) + 10`, with `10 = (ℓ−1)(ℓ−2)/2`) has a monochromatic solution of
`x₁ + ⋯ + x_k = x_{k+1}` with exactly 7 distinct integers. -/
theorem q6_upper (k : Nat) (hk : 6 ≤ k) (c : Nat → Bool) : ExactSol k 6 (natv q6F k) c :=
  kernel_upper 6 6 7 q6V q6Es.flatten q6F q6u q6_u q6E_ok q6_unsat k hk c

